The cannonball is fired from the left and follows a parabolic trajectory. At t=0.00, it is at the launch point. By t=0.13, it is moving right and slightly down. At t=0.23, it is further right and lower. At t=0.37, it is near the center of the screen and descending toward the ground level. The trajectory suggests it will hit the ground (green grass) before reaching any of the robots, since the robots are stacked on the right and the cannonball is moving from left to right and downward.

The cannonball will hit the ground and stop. Since it never hits any robot, no robot is destroyed. All robots remain intact.

