The cannonball is fired from the left and follows a parabolic trajectory. At t=0.00, it is at the launch point. By t=0.13, it is moving right and upward. At t=0.23, it is at the peak of its arc. At t=0.37, it is descending. The trajectory shows it will hit the leftmost structure (containing robots 1 and 2) first, as it is the closest target along its path.

The cannonball will hit the brown wooden block (robot 1) first. Since the block is wooden and the cannonball is a hard projectile, it will likely destroy robot 1 and possibly topple the structure it's part of. The structure with robots 1, 2, and 3 will collapse. Robot 2 is directly below robot 1 and will be pushed down and destroyed. Robot 3, which is on a higher level, will likely be hit by falling debris and destroyed. Robot 4 is on top of the structure and will be hit by falling blocks and destroyed. The right structure with robots 5 and 6 is farther away and will not be hit by the cannonball, so robots 5 and 6 survive.

